# Zone 1, room 9: Reverse pogo (BUILD.md s5 tech 9: "pogo while moving backward to reposition behind an enemy. Taught by a shielded enemy").
# ADR-0010 "Reverse pogo": it takes a dash's speed, a short-hop dash-jump at the enemy and a down-and-back strike, so the room gives a runway
# (x 74 to 766 = 692 u of floor, 77 ticks of running) before the guard and a landing run behind it (1088 to the east strip at 1856 u).
# Stand-in (no shielded enemy exists yet): the guard is a pogo block 32 x 64 u (the training dummy's size) at x 1056..1088, standing on the floor
# (y 960), as in tests/replay/rooms/shield.room; `entity guard` is a marker only (faces=west: the shield side; the back is the east side), nothing
# simulates it. The block is passive: the first encounter is walking up to it with nothing to fear.
# The route: run to x about 780, dash at the guard, dash-jump on dash frame 6 or 7 (vx 5120 = 20 u/f), turn back (stick left) with the
# down-strike on tick 12 or any of the 6 ticks that follow: the bounce keeps the forward speed, Ash sails over the block and lands behind it
# facing it, and walks on to the east door. Fixtures: tests/replay/zone1/09_*.fixture.
# Not the only way across, and why the tech is still the best way to meet the guard: no tech can be required here. A guard standing in the open
# is 64 u tall and a plain jump clears it; the reverse pogo differs from a forward pogo or a jump over it only in which way Ash faces on landing,
# and a door cannot ask that. BUILD.md's reason for the tech, the shielded enemy's unshielded back, needs a combat the Phase 1 stand-ins do not
# have (no enemy blocks a strike yet). What the route with the tech gives is Ash behind the guard facing its back, the one position its
# shield cannot cover; the controls show a forward pogo lands facing away, and a hop at the guard without the dash falls back in front of it.
# (A running jump from the guard's west face with a late strike also lands behind it, facing it: found while building this room, see the feel log.)
room zone1/09_reverse_pogo
size 60 34
spawn 74 960
tiles
